WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Standing in the dark
staring into a mirror

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:04.421
summoning Bloody Mary
by chanting her name

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.340
is a terrifying classic
sleepover ritual.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:08.842
Here's the basic premise.

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.052
If you chant "Bloody Mary"
while looking in a mirror

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:13.555
in a dark room,
preferably a bathroom,

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:17.517
the face of this spectral woman
will appear alongside you.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.520
The mirror is a symbol of
revelation and self-reflection.

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:22.939
It forces us to see
what others see.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.149
In fiction,

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:25.984
mirrors and reflections
often serve as tools

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:29.738
for confrontation like in
"Harry Potter" or "Snow White."

00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:31.406
Even when serving as portals

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:33.116
or windows to
alternative worlds,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.785
like an "Alice Through the
Looking Glass" or "Oculus,"

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.537
the journey of self-discovery

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.331
or revelation is paramount.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.084
[dramatic music]

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.673
With Bloody Mary,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.425
that truth might just
be a good fright,

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:53.428
or her appearance might tell
your future, grant you a wish,

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:55.388
or perhaps even kill you.

00:00:57.682 --> 00:01:01.686
I'm Dr. Emily Zarka
and this is "Monstrum."

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.772
If you were unlucky enough
to summon Bloody Mary,

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:06.191
there's no real standard
of what you'll see.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:08.777
By some accounts, she's
hideously mutilated,

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.696
but in others, she is
beautiful but bloody.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.822
More commonly though,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.617
every aspect of her
appearance is vague.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.912
Her spectral origin story
is all over the place too.

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:21.748
She's tragically disfigured
and out for revenge

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:23.792
or she's been killed
by a jealous lover.

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:25.251
There's even versions where

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:28.004
she was a witch burned
at the stake in Salem.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:28.880
In some legends,

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:30.799
she's connected to a cult.

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:33.176
Where she comes from
and what she looks like

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.721
is less important than the
ritual that summons her.

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:39.224
Three things are
almost always required,

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:42.352
a dark room, a
mirror, and a chant.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.062
You have to say
her name anywhere

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:46.356
from three to 100 times,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.859
and in some accounts, you must
have a single candle burning.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.779
In others, the summoning
must occur in a bathroom.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:55.615
A few tales even specify
you have to run water,

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:58.660
flush the toilet, or
spin around three times.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.620
Still others note
that you must run out

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:03.706
of the room when you see her
or she can cause you harm.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.458
And in some versions
of the legend,

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:07.961
you even have to
offer your own blood.

00:02:08.044 --> 00:02:09.295
What happens from there?

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.922
She might reveal your future,

00:02:11.005 --> 00:02:13.341
but in most stories
she's threatening.

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:16.135
She will frighten you out of
the room or even attack you

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:17.512
in the real world.

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:19.722
In one particularly
gruesome variation,

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.349
if you touch the mirror,

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:24.435
she'll be able to drag you
into her realm and kill you.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:25.979
Sound ambiguous?

00:02:26.062 --> 00:02:28.940
Yeah, that's kind of the
point, at least in my mind.

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:31.109
Not knowing exactly
what is going to happen

00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:32.443
or who is going to appear

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:34.612
in the mirror is part
of the attraction

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:37.657
of this legend, and a
reason to try it yourself.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.993
There are three common
elements to the legend.

00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:41.369
Let's break it down.

00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:42.954
First, the dark room.

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:45.039
Fact, it's scary
to be in the dark,

00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:46.291
especially if you're asking

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:48.084
for something
supernatural to happen.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.587
Our eyes tend to play
tricks on us in the dark.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.297
Seeing a distorted
reflection in the mirror is

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.300
possible when darkness and
flickering light are in play.

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:56.718
In the case of Bloody Mary,

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.512
overall spookiness and fear
are common culprits too.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.139
Second, the mirror.

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:03.349
Mirrors serve as
symbolic boundaries,

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:05.184
spaces where the
real is confronted

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:06.311
while offering the possibility

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:09.939
of alternative ways
of seeing or being.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.901
After all, there is the
idea of the mirror realm.

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:14.527
The basic concept
of the mirror realm

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:16.195
is that there is an opposite,

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:18.990
usually darker world that
exists alongside our own.

00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:21.951
And mirrors serve as the
portals between the two.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.579
Even before bloody Mary
entered into the picture,

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:27.540
the idea existed that
with some kind of ritual,

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:31.294
otherworldly figures could
appear inside of mirrors.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.712
In some lore,

00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:35.298
a malicious magic practitioner
could even bind a spirit

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.300
or the devil to a mirror.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.303
As a threat of real persecution
for witchcraft declined,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.181
the idea of a cult play
or lighthearted dabbling

00:03:43.264 --> 00:03:46.643
in a cult and magical
practices rose in popularity.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.686
Young adults,
particularly women,

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.022
turned to the mirror
for divination rituals,

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:54.651
often with the intention of
identifying their future spouse.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.111
Knowledge of these playful
rituals was popular enough

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:57.904
that in the early 20th century,

00:03:57.987 --> 00:03:59.739
as the postcard industry boomed,

00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:02.450
cards depicting women engaging

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:04.369
in divination
rituals were popular

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:08.247
during the fall season, often
corresponding to Halloween.

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:09.707
In one example,

00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:11.751
a girl stands in front of
mirrors holding a candle

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.419
while the nebulous face

00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:16.214
of a handsome male figure
appears over her shoulder.

00:04:16.297 --> 00:04:19.634
But not all cards show
such appealing prospects.

00:04:19.717 --> 00:04:20.969
Other versions show
a stereotypical witch

00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:23.680
or the frightening
ghost of a man.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.431
Connecting the
mirror ritual back

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:27.767
to its more nefarious
associations.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.019
It's hard to guess
how seriously rituals

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.479
like these were taken.

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:33.731
Although the playful
commodification of the events

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:37.193
suggests at least some level
of carefree participation.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:38.861
The mirror ritual offers a form

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:42.073
of boundary rebellion with
little risk of true danger,

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:44.534
an appealing prospect
for teenagers.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.868
And finally, the chant,

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.787
or what puts the
Mary in Bloody Mary.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:51.833
The repeated name is
always a female one,

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.209
Bloody Mary of course,

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:56.295
but also Mary Worth,
Mary Ruth, Black Madame,

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.797
Mary Lou, Mary Johnson,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.341
Mary Weather, and Mary
Whales, for example.

00:05:00.425 --> 00:05:02.218
Mary is a common name,

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:03.428
but some of these
women stand out

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.346
more than others in folklore.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.807
Take Mary Worth, for example,
said to have a disfigured face

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.435
either from genetics
or a bad accident,

00:05:10.518 --> 00:05:12.395
she resented her looks.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.856
So much so that she put
a curse upon the mirror

00:05:14.939 --> 00:05:18.818
she gazed into one day, and
it shattered, killing her.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.320
If you stare into a mirror
and summon Mary Worth,

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:22.697
she will appear at a distance

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.699
in the reflection moving closer

00:05:24.782 --> 00:05:27.326
and closer until she
shatters the mirror.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.786
And if this happens,

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.872
you'll never again be
able to look into a mirror

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:33.124
without seeing her reflection.

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:35.043
Or there's Mary Whales.

00:05:35.126 --> 00:05:37.128
This Mary was a young
woman who was killed

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:39.047
when she was run
over by a truck.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.590
Six years after she died,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.633
a couple saw her
trying to hitchhike.

00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:45.636
Bleeding and wet, she had
scratches on her face.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.056
You can look in a mirror and
summon her ghost by saying

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:49.974
"I do believe in Mary Whales"

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:51.851
somewhere between
10 or 100 times.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.520
Given the hitchhiking
ghost element,

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:56.773
this urban legend might
be a regional variant

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.776
combining elements of
other legends and monsters,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:03.780
like the vanishing hitchhiker,
La Llorona, or Mary Worth.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.115
And let's address the
royal elephant in the room.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.742
Only one other female figure

00:06:07.825 --> 00:06:09.911
in history has been
called Bloody Mary,

00:06:09.994 --> 00:06:12.497
Mary Tudor or Queen Mary I.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.626
Born to Katherine of Aragon
and King Henry VIII in 1516,

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:19.420
princess Mary was named
after her beautiful aunt,

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.672
an attribute she came to embody.

00:06:21.756 --> 00:06:24.008
Scorned by her father
upon his second marriage,

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:26.511
she would eventually be
declared his rightful heir

00:06:26.594 --> 00:06:28.846
in his will and took
the throne in 1553.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.516
Her reign was
fraught with tension.

00:06:31.599 --> 00:06:32.809
At Mary's command,

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:34.852
hundreds of Protestants
were burned at the stake

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:36.062
as heretics.

00:06:36.145 --> 00:06:37.605
Despite this violence,

00:06:37.688 --> 00:06:40.316
it wasn't until her half
Sister Queen Elizabeth's rule

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.527
that she would become
known as Bloody Mary,

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.445
likely as an attempt to diminish

00:06:44.529 --> 00:06:47.406
or at least tarnish her
historical significance.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.908
The catchy name
gained popularity

00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:51.035
as the 17th century wore on.

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.871
So by the time the infamous
mirror summoning postcards

00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:55.873
popped up in the 20th century,

00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:57.875
the nickname had been around
for hundreds of years.

00:06:57.959 --> 00:06:59.919
To me, there seems to
be an easy connection

00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:02.922
between the royal
and real Bloody Mary

00:07:03.005 --> 00:07:04.549
and the folkloric monster.

00:07:04.632 --> 00:07:05.883
Both of their stories deal

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:07.927
with the cultural
perception of beauty

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:10.763
and of stories being rewritten
by whomever is telling them,

00:07:10.847 --> 00:07:14.016
casting the Marys as both
victims and villains.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.643
When we consider
where the summoning

00:07:15.726 --> 00:07:17.270
of Bloody Mary often occurs,

00:07:17.353 --> 00:07:20.398
in bathrooms, and by
whom, young women,

00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:22.567
another interpretation
becomes apparent.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.111
Bathrooms are uniquely
liminal places.

00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:26.988
Whether private or public,
they are rooms

00:07:27.071 --> 00:07:30.324
within larger spaces
where private acts occur--

00:07:30.408 --> 00:07:33.744
bodily functions often
seen as gross or taboo.

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:36.789
Folklorist Alan Dundes'
freudian reading of Bloody Mary

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:39.083
proposes a metaphorical
representation

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:41.210
to the onset of menstruation.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.171
He argues that the
mirror summoning ritual

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:45.798
serves as a right of
passage into puberty,

00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:47.675
a journey that is both
feared and celebrated.

00:07:47.758 --> 00:07:50.887
If we accept this
reading of the legend,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.263
then bloody Mary is a warning,

00:07:52.346 --> 00:07:54.223
not only about the inevitability

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.517
of the sudden bleeding
women will likely deal with

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:59.896
in the bathroom,
but of puberty in general.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:02.565
An adolescent girl gazing
in the mirror may be met

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.275
with both trepidation and wonder

00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:06.319
at her own changing appearance.

00:08:06.402 --> 00:08:08.112
And that's before you
factor in the pressures

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:11.073
of an entire beauty industry
dedicated to making her

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.826
want to alter the reflection
staring back at her.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.579
Not to mention the expectations
of whatever standard

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.790
of attractiveness is being
promoted in culture at the time.

00:08:19.874 --> 00:08:22.210
Perhaps then, it is
unsurprising that the Mary

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:25.087
in the mirror is always
frightening when summoned.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.714
It also helps explain
why Bloody Mary

00:08:26.797 --> 00:08:28.716
is a common figure
at sleepovers,

00:08:28.799 --> 00:08:30.468
which often occur during puberty

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:32.053
and into the teen years.

00:08:32.136 --> 00:08:34.347
Telling scary stories,
playing games,

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.849
and pulling pranks are
all common at sleepovers,

00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:38.517
at least the ones I went to.

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:40.645
And Bloody Mary is an
option that can fit

00:08:40.728 --> 00:08:44.023
into all three categories
for just the right age group.

00:08:44.106 --> 00:08:45.900
It's worth noting
that the participant

00:08:45.983 --> 00:08:49.445
in the Bloody Mary ritual
is always in control,

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:51.113
or appears to be.

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.907
They're the one
who says the name,

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.826
but they can also turn on
the lights or run away.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:59.205
The ghost is summoned. It
does not simply appear.

00:08:59.288 --> 00:09:02.500
Unlike other monstrous spectral
encounters or ghostly women

00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:04.627
like the Banshee or La Llorona,

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.005
this notorious female
specter must be invited in,

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:10.258
which partially
diminishes her power,

00:09:10.341 --> 00:09:11.759
or at least her reach,

00:09:11.842 --> 00:09:13.719
and removes some of
Bloody Mary's potential

00:09:13.803 --> 00:09:15.012
to cause terror.

00:09:15.096 --> 00:09:17.181
So our ability to
control the appearance

00:09:17.265 --> 00:09:20.309
of Bloody Mary takes a little
bit of the danger out of it.

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.603
Fear becomes fun.

00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:26.357
The idea existed that with
some kind of ritual...

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.526
Some kind of ritual, pause.

00:09:28.609 --> 00:09:30.653
(crew)
Rolling by the way, but...

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:31.946
Ooh, cut that.

